{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UZnnVRZfe2mQMg9j6yrKoH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state:**\n- `pkg/format/` has source code on the working branch (color.go, column.go, size.go)\n- `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/testutils/`, and all `cmd/` packages have no source code on the working branch\n- All specs through release 01.3 are written; code generation has not run on this branch\n\n**Current release (00.0):** Foundational infrastructure. Four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles — excluded from generation (DD7)\n- uc002-format — source code already exists\n- **uc003-sys — needs implementation**\n- **uc004-testutils — needs implementation**\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 has two remaining generation targets: `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/testutils/`. By canonical ordering (alphabetical path tiebreaker between peer libraries), `pkg/sys/` comes first. Additionally, `pkg/format/color.go:124` has a TODO noting that `isTerminal` should delegate to `pkg/sys.IsTerminal` (prd003-format R2.3), making `pkg/sys/` a direct dependency of existing code. Implementation and tests must be separate tasks per P2; with a 1-task limit, the implementation task comes first.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/sys/ terminal detection and stat abstraction -- rel00.0-uc003-sys\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys/ component description, technology choices for golang.org/x/sys, design decision DD4)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (glob for prd*sys*.yaml and read the full PRD -- follow its requirement IDs and design choices verbatim)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (uc003-sys section)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (lines 119-128: local isTerminal stub using raw syscall that should delegate to pkg/sys.IsTerminal per prd003-format R2.3)\n      - go.mod (confirm golang.org/x/sys dependency is declared)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: IsTerminal and GetWinSize functions wrapping TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat.go\n        action: create\n        note: Stat and Lstat wrappers returning platform-independent FileInfo type\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: Darwin-specific Stat_t field accessors (Mtimespec, Blocks)\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: Linux-specific Stat_t field accessors (Mtim, Blocks)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool using the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix. This is the function pkg/format/color.go's local isTerminal (line 124) must delegate to. Cross-reference: prd003-format R2.3.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement GetWinSize(fd uintptr) (rows int, cols int, err error) querying terminal dimensions via the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl using golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement Stat(path string) and Lstat(path string) returning a FileInfo struct that provides Mtime() time.Time and Blocks() int64, abstracting the Darwin st_mtimespec vs Linux st_mtim and st_blocks field-name divergence.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Use Go build constraints (//go:build darwin and //go:build linux) to isolate platform-specific unix.Stat_t field access into stat_darwin.go and stat_linux.go. terminal.go and stat.go contain only platform-independent logic.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"golang.org/x/sys/unix is the only import for syscall access (per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology choices). Do not use the syscall package directly for anything golang.org/x/sys covers. cmd/ packages must not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- they use pkg/sys/.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Platform divergence is isolated via Go build tags. Only stat field accessors diverge between Darwin and Linux; terminal ioctl calls are identical across both platforms via x/sys/unix and do not need platform-specific files.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Only wrap syscalls that have platform divergence or that Go's standard library does not expose cleanly (per ARCHITECTURE.yaml pkg/sys/ component: 'Only syscalls that have platform divergence between Darwin and Linux, or that Go standard library does not expose cleanly, belong here'). os.Stat is insufficient because it does not expose Stat_t.Blocks or raw mtime with nanosecond precision portably.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/sys/... succeeds on the current platform with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/... passes with no warnings.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"No direct imports of the syscall package anywhere in pkg/sys/ -- only golang.org/x/sys/unix.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"All exported functions and types have doc comments referencing the PRD requirement they implement.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"FileInfo accessors return correct types: Mtime() time.Time, Blocks() int64.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19176,"cache_read_input_tokens":19285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19176},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1520cfbb-de6e-40e4-a548-0abf5ae4ad37","uuid":"64410cda-7ba0-420f-849e-f3dd9ddc1a50"}
